[72.234,"o","\u001b[2m# What the stack published: URL and credentials, as secrets in the stack's vault, base64 (OPENVIDU_URL appears once\r\n# OpenVidu serves: until then this read fails, and ov waits for it).\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[72.234,"o","$ "]
[72.234,"o","VAULT=\"$(terraform -chdir=.openvidu/oracle output -raw vault_id)\"\r\n"]
[72.663,"m","The runbook's commands, exactly as ov printed them 6/6"]
[72.663,"o","$ "]
[72.665,"o","oci secrets secret-bundle get-secret-bundle-by-name --secret-name OPENVIDU_URL --vault-id $VAULT --query 'data.\"secret-bundle-content\".content' --raw-output --region eu-madrid-1 | base64 -d\r\n"]
[73.303,"o","https://openvidu-mwgjh3-51-170-58-250.sslip.io/"]
[73.473,"m","The same command again: ov finds the machines and ends the deploy, creating nothing"]
[73.473,"o","$ "]
[73.474,"o","ov stack deploy openvidu-e2e-oci-ce-s125537 --cloud oracle --mode assisted\r\n"]
[74.526,"o","warning: the stack publishes into the vault *** (--oci-vault), which is not its own. Its secrets have fixed names (OPENVIDU_URL, the credentials, the license, the stack's access), so two stacks in one vault mix them; every deploy adds versions to the same secrets until Oracle refuses more (LimitExceeded) and the stack never publishes; and a destroy leaves this stack's credentials in it. Give every stack a vault of its own: leave --oci-vault out and the stack creates one\r\n"]
[74.527,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so the command that continues this deploy needs no flags\r\n"]
